course: dictionary
lesson: 11816
title: Two sides, one word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are built from smaller parts, and the parts give clues. Bilateral is made of bi, which means two, and lateral, which means side. Put them together and bilateral means involving two sides.
explain: «The two countries signed a bilateral agreement about trade.» Both countries are on the agreement, so bilateral means between two sides, not many. Check it by swapping in your meaning: «The two countries signed a two-sided agreement about trade.» It still makes sense.
explain: In science, bilateral means having to do with both sides of the body. «Humans and butterflies show bilateral symmetry.» Their left and right halves are mirror images, so if you fold them down the middle, the two halves match.
fact: Bilateral means involving two sides, groups or countries.
fact: Bi means two, and lateral means side.
fact: In science, bilateral means having to do with both sides of the body.
fact: Bilateral symmetry means the left and right halves are mirror images of each other.
fact: Bilateral is a formal word, and you will often meet it in news about politics and in science lessons.
exercise: «The two countries signed a bilateral agreement.» What does bilateral mean here? | Involving many countries | *Involving two sides | Very old | Sung loudly
exercise: «Butterflies show bilateral symmetry.» What does bilateral symmetry mean? | *The left and right halves are mirror images | The wings are made of glass | The butterfly can fly backwards | Both halves are very different
exercise: In bilateral, the part bi means how many? | Many | *Two | One hundred | Three
test: «The meeting was bilateral, with only the leaders of two nations.» What does bilateral mean in this sentence? | *Between two sides only | Open to everyone in the world | Very quiet and private | Held outdoors in the rain
test: Which of these is an example of bilateral symmetry? | *A butterfly with matching wings on each side | A cloud shaped by the wind | A ball that rolls freely down a hill | A pile of loose stones
exam: Ava says, «The talks are bilateral», and her friend asks what it means. What is the best reply? | The talks are about the weather | *Only two sides are taking part | Everybody in the school is taking part | The talks are very short
